*.swp

# Docker volumes (local dev)
pgdata/

# Stray secrets — defensive guardrail; censprobe itself never writes these
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# .env is intentionally tracked — it ships safe defaults that work out of
# the box (localhost-only services). Local edits live in your working
# tree; only push them if you really mean to publish them.
# reports/ and targets/ are tracked (they're the product).
# Credentials never touch disk (cred_server hands them over a one-shot
# TLS endpoint), so no per-protocol-yaml ignore rule is needed.
